  "query_preview": "After a weak cold front passage temperatures today\nwill be cooler than yesterday but values will still be above\nnormal. Well above normal temperatures with highs nearly 10 to\n15 degrees above normal are likely to prevail through much of\nthe upcoming week. Some locations east of the Divide may see\nhighs flirt with 80 throughout much of the week which is quite\nunprecedented for October. As mentioned in the previous\ndiscussion these warm temperatures and dry conditions may lead\nto prolonged periods of elevated fire weather conditions through\nthe upcoming week. Long range forecast models are hinting at the\nwarmth eventually breaking down by the end of next week into the\nweekend. However, being nearly a week out there remains high\nuncertainty. For now, well above normal temperatures and dry\nconditions look to persist across the region for the near\nfuture.",
